$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure 2: Oxidation of the alcohols
to the aldehydes 1-4. The alcohol S4 a-d (1.0 eq.) was dissolved in DMSO
(10mL/mmol) and 2-iodoxybenzoic acid (IBX, 1.5 eq.) was added. After
stirring for 12h at rt, the mixture was added to DCM and washed with dem.
water (3x), saturated NaHCO3 (aq) (3x) and brine (2x). Evaporation gives
the corresponding aldehyde without the need for further purification.
(3S)-tert-Butyl
3-((S)-2-(((benzyloxy)carbonyl)amino)-4-methylpentanamido)-4-
oxo-4-((1-oxopropan-2-yl)amino)butanoate (2). (3S)-tert-Butyl
3-((S)-2-(((benzyloxy)carbonyl)amino)-4-methylpentanamido)-4-
oxo-4-((1-oxopentan-2-yl)amino)butanoate (4). General procedure 2; yield:
85.0%, colorless oil, mixture of diasteromers. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3,
300 K): δ [ppm] = 9.47 (1H, s), 7.50 (1NH, m), 7.33 (5H, m), 5.31 (1NH,
m), 5.06 (2H, m), 4.83 (1H, m), 4.33 (1H, m), 4.10 (1H, m), 2.81 (2H, m),
1.81 (1H, m), 1.60 (5H, m), 1.44 (9H, s), 1.36 (1H, m), 0.94 (6H, m),
0.84 (3H, m). 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K): δ [ppm] = 200.03, 172.57,
171.70, 171.04, 156.94, 136.22, 128.91, 128.63, 128.34, 82.31, 67.63,
59.07, 54.74, 49.54, 41.11, 36.80, 30.84, 28.31, 25.12, 23.07, 22.14,
18.89, 14.43. HPLC: tR = 6.10 min. ESI-MS: m/z = 542.
